      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 4 4\n1 5 4 4\n5 4 3\n1 4 3 3 5\n4 3 1\n3 1 3 9",
        "output": "2\n2\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: One way of using two blimps is as follows:\n\nInitially, A=[1,5,4,4]A = [1, 5, 4, 4]A=[1,5,4,4]\nShower confetti on city 222. Now, A=[−3,1,4,4]A = [-3, 1, 4, 4]A=[−3,1,4,4].\nShower confetti on city 444. Now, A=[−7,−3,0,0]A = [-7, -3, 0, 0]A=[−7,−3,0,0] and we are done.\n\nTest case 222: One way of using two blimps is as follows:\n\nInitially, A=[1,4,3,3,5]A = [1, 4, 3, 3, 5]A=[1,4,3,3,5]\nLet a blimp fly over every city. Now, A=[−2,1,0,0,2]A = [-2, 1, 0, 0, 2]A=[−2,1,0,0,2].\nShower confetti on city 555. Now, A=[−5,−2,−3,−3,−2]A = [-5, -2, -3, -3, -2]A=[−5,−2,−3,−3,−2], and we are done."
      }
    ]
